    {
      "cve": {
        "id": "CVE-2026-109138",
        "sourceIdentifier": "30a5e7fb-040d-440a-8cdf-a4a2068ce72e",
        "published": "2026-11-17T09:17:26.057",
        "lastModified": "2026-11-17T17:17:47.680",
        "vulnStatus": "Received",
        "cveTags": [],
        "descriptions": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "value": "In the Aliro access control reference\n  applications of the Nordic Semiconductor nRF Door Lock and Access Control\n  Add-on v1.0.0 through v1.1.1, built with Credential Issuer CA\n  certificate-based issuer trust (CONFIG_DOOR_LOCK_CREDENTIAL_ISSUER_CA) and\n  the Aliro Step-up phase (CONFIG_DOOR_LOCK_STEP_UP_PHASE) enabled,\n  AccessManagerImpl::ProcessValidityIteration() treats a failed lookup of the\n  Credential Issuer in the provisioned issuer array as success. For an issuer\n  trusted through a certificate chain but not provisioned, the\n  ValidityIteration (credential-rollback) check is therefore skipped. A former\n  authorized holder with an old but correctly issuer-signed Access Document can\n  be granted physical access after the issuer has advanced its iteration to\n  revoke that credential. The default Matter provisioning configuration is not\n  affected. Fixed in v1.2.0."
          }
        ],
        "affected": [
